  "limits": [
    "The existing unsafeWindow/GM and page-first auto implementation was hardened; default/content isolation, raw unwrap, matching and native authorization policy are unchanged. This is not full Violentmonkey parity or a new page isolation boundary.",
    "Trusted navigation suspends startup and connections. Unsent work is canceled and stale reads/snapshots discarded. Submitted storage/cookie writes retain real completion status while the bridge is usable; a lost bridge can still leave the outcome uncertain. No submitted operation is replayed.",
    "All three final userscript runs restored a cached document and retained one source execution with fresh values/menus. Real Chromium worker restarts were tested in Edge/Chrome; Firefox uses its background document. No mobile/browser crashes, live third-party scripts or production websites were tested.",
    "Eight regressions were reproduced before their fixes: seven lifecycle tests plus document-body observer retention at retry exhaustion. Intermediate tests caught cookie acknowledgement compatibility, which was preserved in the final implementation.",
    "The first Edge feature fixture had an incorrect menuId lookup; it was corrected to id. Early passing Edge/Chrome feature runs preceded the final terminal-cleanup change and are retained as pre-final.",
    "The first combined Edge run reached MCP network reads but raced asynchronous helper disconnect before requesting a new pairing code. The test helper now waits for the observed disconnected state; the final Edge run recorded one wait. Production MCP code is unchanged.",
    "Combined suites cover matching, editor/external files, installs, GM storage/menus, DOM/tab helpers, dependencies/HTTP, page-world execution, both read-only MCP transports and local blocked-ad canaries. They do not perform OS clipboard writes, desktop notifications or the separate large-download suite.",
    "Manifest, blockers/rules and the native broker are byte-identical to the starting snapshot. The full Edge blocker suite also passed. Disposable test profiles and deny proxies isolate every browser run."
  ],
